                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Remember the three essential components of a conventional core biopsy needle:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Stylet: carries the sampling notch."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Sampling notch: receives the tissue."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Cutting cannula: severs the tissue core."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The key distinction from FNA is that core biopsy preserves tissue architecture, making it especially useful when histological diagnosis and assessment of invasion are required."
